  "version": "1.0",
  "changes_html": "<h2>About This Vintage</h2><h2>Changes Since the Last Update</h2><p>Since the <a href=\"https://budgetlab.yale.edu/research/state-us-tariffs-may-12-2025\">May 12 report</a>:</p><ul><li>President Trump announced a 50% tariff on the EU to take effect on June 1. TBL interprets this policy as a expansion of the 10% &lsquo;reciprocal&rsquo; tariff rate currently levied on the EU, first announced on April 2 and modified April 9.</li></ul><p>TBL analyzes tariffs on a &ldquo;real-time current policy&rdquo; basis, where policy as it stands as of date certain is assumed to continue in perpetuity, even if framed as a temporary policy.</p>",
